#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0570 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0570 (Rule: ARM not in ('Screen Failure', 'Not Assigned', 'Unplanned Treatment', 'Not Treated')). Row 2 records the screen failure in ARM (ARM = Screen Failure) instead of ARMNRS -> fires; row 3 uses NOT ASSIGNED in upper case, which the check compares case-insensitively -> fires. Row 1 (Placebo) and row 4 (ARM empty, reason in ARMNRS) are silent."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=S1-002 ARM="Screen Failure"
#expectViolationAt row=3 USUBJID=S1-003 ARM="NOT ASSIGNED"
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ARMNRS  type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | PBO  | Placebo        |
S1 | DM | S1-002 | SCRNFAIL | Screen Failure |
S1 | DM | S1-003 | NOTASSGN | NOT ASSIGNED   |
S1 | DM | S1-004 |      |                | SCREEN FAILURE
